; A signature's AXTAG belongs to ITS OWN function, and to no other of
; the same bare name.
;
; `checkAxtags` folds in the tags of the signature declaring the same
; function (see 341). The first version of that lookup matched with
; `nameMatches` against the BARE name, and `nameMatches "TagNone$work"
; "work"` answers true - so `TagPure`'s `pure` claim was applied to
; `TagNone`'s `work` as well, and `TagNone` drew a warning at its own
; line for a claim its file does not contain.
;
; Exactly one AX3010 is correct here: `mangleDecl` rewrites a
; TAG_D_SIG and a TAG_D_FN alike, so a function and its own signature
; agree exactly and the lookup can be - and now is - an exact match.
(import TagPure)
(import TagNone)
(:: main Int)
(fn (main) 0)
